<!-- ============ DEMO ============ -->
<section class="demo" style="border-top:0;padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <figure class="film plate reg-b">
      <figcaption class="cap"><span>Fig. 00 · the skill at work</span><span>17s · no sound</span></figcaption>
      <video id="demo" muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="Demo: a prompt typed in an agent session becomes an architecture diagram, then a before and after, then the 44 diagram types." width="1920" height="1080"></video>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ BEFORE / AFTER ============ -->
<section id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">The model had the content.<br>It was missing the taste.</h2>
      <p class="note rise">Same content, two passes: Claude on its own, then Claude with the skill.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ba">
      <div class="fig rise" data-full="assets/before.png" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="View the first-pass diagram full size">
        <div class="lab"><span>Fig. 02a</span><span class="n">First pass · no skill</span></div>
        <picture class="plate">
          <source srcset="assets/before.webp" type="image/webp">
          <img src="assets/before.png" alt="A first-pass lifecycle diagram from Claude with no skill: six identical white cards in a row with blue number badges, and a dark bar underneath reading AI plus Governance plus Humans." width="1600" height="389" loading="lazy">
        </picture>
        <span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span>
      </div>
      <div class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <span>REDRAWN</span>
      </div>
      <div class="fig fix rise" data-full="assets/after-dark.png" data-full-light="assets/after-light.png" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="View the redrawn diagram full size">
        <div class="lab"><span>Fig. 02b</span><span class="n">Redrawn with the skill</span></div>
        <picture class="plate reg-b only-dark">
          <source srcset="assets/after-dark.webp" type="image/webp">
          <img src="assets/after-dark.png" alt="The same lifecycle redrawn with the skill: six stages from Idea to Run and Change, each with an Intent, Guardrail and Outcome row, Triage as the one highlighted stage, and an operating model strip underneath." width="1600" height="915" loading="lazy">
        </picture>
        <picture class="plate reg-b only-light">
          <source srcset="assets/after-light.webp" type="image/webp">
          <img src="assets/after-light.png" alt="The same lifecycle redrawn with the skill: six stages from Idea to Run and Change, each with an Intent, Guardrail and Outcome row, Triage as the one highlighted stage, and an operating model strip underneath." width="1600" height="915" loading="lazy">
        </picture>
        <span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ul class="deltas rise">
      <li><b>One accent, not six.</b> Color points at the single node that matters, nothing else.</li>
      <li><b>Real hierarchy.</b> Type weight and grouping carry the meaning, not a rainbow of fills.</li>
      <li><b>Structure you can read.</b> Every stage answers the same three questions: intent, guardrail, outcome. Read across a row and you see the whole system.</li>
    </ul>
    <blockquote class="quote rise">
      <p>“The model already understood the content. What it was missing was taste, so I wrote the taste down.”</p>
      <cite>Cathryn Lavery · a generic tool asks “where should this box go?” This one asks “does this box deserve to exist?”</cite>
    </blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ WHAT IT IS (legend) ============ -->
<section id="what">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">What you get</h2>
      <p class="note rise">It runs inside the agent you already use. Nothing new to open, nothing to export.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="legend">
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="10" height="7"/><rect x="19" y="4" width="10" height="7"/><rect x="3" y="21" width="10" height="7"/><rect x="19" y="21" width="10" height="7"/></svg><h3>50 visual types</h3></div>
        <p>Architecture, Sankey, heatmap, exploded axonometric, database schema and more. Each is a real type with its own rules, not one box style restyled 50 ways.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="M16 16l11 11"/><path d="M8 11h6M11 8v6"/></svg><h3>Brand-matched in ~60s</h3></div>
        <p>Point it at your site. It reads your colors and fonts and applies them to every diagram it draws.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="4" width="22" height="24"/><path d="M9 10h14M9 15h14M9 20h9"/></svg><h3>Self-contained HTML + SVG</h3></div>
        <p>One file. Opens double-clicked, offline. No build step, no dashboard, nothing to host.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 8h9l3 3h8v13H6z"/><path d="M12 18l4 4 5-6"/></svg><h3>Imports draw.io, Mermaid &amp; Excalidraw</h3></div>
        <p>Point it at a source and it <em>redraws</em> (not converts) at the size, detail and audience your destination needs.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 16h6l3-8 6 16 3-8h6"/></svg><h3>Optional accessible motion</h3></div>
        <p>Diagrams can animate when it helps the explanation. Static is the default.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="spec rise">
        <div><div class="row"><svg class="g" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="12"/><path d="M16 9v7l5 3"/></svg><h3>Accessible by default</h3></div>
        <p>Screen readers announce each diagram’s title and description, not a blank rectangle.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ AXONOMETRIC ============ -->
<section id="axonometric">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">New: two axonometric types</h2>
      <p class="note rise">One 2:1 projection, two jobs. Static by default, with animated examples.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="axo">
      <div class="axo-item rise">
        <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/exploded.png" aria-label="View the Exploded axonometric diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Exploded axonometric</span><span>Fig. 04a</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/exploded.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/exploded.png" alt="Exploded view of a three-layer app stack: data at the base, logic in the middle, interface on top, with logic as the focal layer." width="2400" height="1336" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span></button>
        <h3>Exploded axonometric</h3>
        <p>Parts of one object pulled apart along one axis: a teardown, an unboxing, assembly order. Every part sits at an equal gap, and every coordinate comes from one projection function.</p>
        <ul class="axo-links">
          <li><a href="examples/exploded.html">App stack</a></li>
          <li><a href="examples/exploded-phone.html">Phone teardown</a></li>
          <li><a href="examples/exploded-unboxing.html">Unboxing</a></li>
          <li class="live"><a href="examples/exploded-phone-animated.html">Phone, animated</a></li>
          <li class="live"><a href="examples/exploded-unboxing-animated.html">Unboxing, animated</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="axo-item rise">
        <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/axonometric-plan.png" aria-label="View the Axonometric plan diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Axonometric plan</span><span>Fig. 04b</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/axonometric-plan.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/axonometric-plan.png" alt="Axonometric floor plan of an office level with an open office, meeting room, kitchen, lobby, and phone booth, with the meeting room as the focal room." width="2400" height="1078" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span></button>
        <h3>Axonometric plan</h3>
        <p>One floor or site seen from above at an angle: rooms with furniture, buildings by phase. Walls are cut at desk height so every room reads from a single view.</p>
        <ul class="axo-links">
          <li><a href="examples/axonometric-plan.html">Office floor</a></li>
          <li><a href="examples/axonometric-plan-campus.html">Campus</a></li>
          <li class="live"><a href="examples/axonometric-plan-campus-animated.html">Campus by phase, animated</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ GALLERY ============ -->
<section id="gallery">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">Fifty diagrams, one system</h2>
      <a class="note rise" href="https://cathrynlavery.github.io/diagram-design/" style="color:var(--accent)">Browse the live gallery →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="plates">
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/architecture.png" aria-label="View the Architecture diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Architecture</span><span>01 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/architecture.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/architecture.png" alt="Architecture diagram showing reader requests moving through Cloudflare to an Astro origin, MDX bundle, and content CMS." width="2400" height="1154" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Components + connections in one system snapshot</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/architecture-delta.png" aria-label="View the Architecture delta diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Architecture delta</span><span>02 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/architecture-delta.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/architecture-delta.png" alt="Architecture delta for order fulfilment: a durable order queue replaces the legacy dispatcher, Orders API moves from v1 to v2, and seven component and relationship changes are listed between the before and after snapshots." width="2400" height="1362" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Structural change between synchronized Before / After topologies, with a Changes ledger</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/it-state.png" aria-label="View the IT current-state diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">IT current-state</span><span>03 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/it-state.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/it-state.png" alt="Three zones show collection, processing, and dissemination through manual file handoffs." width="2400" height="1252" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Legacy IT landscape by phase or department; shows the before state</span></button>
