      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/data-flow.png" aria-label="View the Data flow diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Data flow</span><span>32 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/data-flow.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/data-flow.png" alt="A Data Engineer ingests and stores commerce data, a Data Scientist transforms and analyzes it, and an Analyst publishes a dashboard." width="2400" height="1176" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Role-scoped data flow: who does what at each pipeline step</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/dp-integration.png" aria-label="View the DP integration diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">DP integration</span><span>33 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/dp-integration.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/dp-integration.png" alt="Integration topology showing CRM, POS exports, and an event stream landing in object storage for query, notebooks, dashboards, and a partner API." width="2400" height="1330" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Integration topology of a data platform: sources → core → consumers</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/dp-security-matrix.png" aria-label="View the DP security matrix diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">DP security matrix</span><span>34 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/dp-security-matrix.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/dp-security-matrix.png" alt="A five by five permission matrix for platform roles and components." width="2400" height="888" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Per-role / per-component access permissions matrix</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/sankey.png" aria-label="View the Sankey diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Sankey</span><span>35 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/sankey.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/sankey.png" alt="Sankey diagram showing 12,000 monthly CI minutes splitting into unit test, E2E, build, and lint stages, then merging into passed, failed, and flaked outcomes, with the flaky-rerun path highlighted as the one accent flow." width="2400" height="1346" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">A quantity splitting and merging across stages, band width = amount</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/fishbone.png" aria-label="View the Fishbone diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Fishbone</span><span>36 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/fishbone.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/fishbone.png" alt="Fishbone diagram tracing a checkout latency incident to five candidate cause categories, with a missing database index under Data confirmed as the root cause." width="2640" height="1072" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Causes of one observed effect, grouped by category (root-cause analysis)</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/wardley.png" aria-label="View the Wardley map diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Wardley map</span><span>37 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/wardley.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/wardley.png" alt="Wardley map plotting an AI assistant product's value chain from the user-facing need down to raw infrastructure against genesis-to-commodity evolution, with agent orchestration commoditising toward the product band." width="2400" height="1106" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Value chain against evolution: what to build, buy, and what is moving</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/kanban.png" aria-label="View the Kanban diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Kanban</span><span>38 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/kanban.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/kanban.png" alt="Kanban board showing a platform team's work-in-progress across backlog, in-progress, review, and done columns, with the in-progress column over its WIP limit and one blocked card awaiting a vendor maintenance window." width="2400" height="946" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Work-in-progress by state, with WIP limits and blocked items</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/journey.png" aria-label="View the User journey diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">User journey</span><span>39 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/journey.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/journey.png" alt="User journey map of a new trial user across five stages, showing actions, touchpoints, and a sentiment curve that dips at the usage-limit stage before recovering at upgrade." width="2560" height="1110" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">What a person does across stages of an experience, and how it feels</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/deployment.png" aria-label="View the Deployment diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Deployment</span><span>40 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/deployment.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/deployment.png" alt="Deployment diagram placing the checkout service across an edge CDN zone, a production Kubernetes zone running ingress and API pods, and a data zone with a primary Postgres instance replicating to a standby." width="2400" height="962" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Where software runs: zones, hosts, artifacts, replicas, ports</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/dependency.png" aria-label="View the Dependency graph diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Dependency graph</span><span>41 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/dependency.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/dependency.png" alt="Ranked dependency graph of a TypeScript monorepo showing shared-types as the highest fan-in package with four dependents, and one back-edge cycle from utils into shared-types." width="2400" height="1442" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">What depends on what, with fan-in and cycles a tree cannot express</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/uml-class.png" aria-label="View the UML class diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">UML class</span><span>42 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/uml-class.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/uml-class.png" alt="Class diagram showing Card and BankTransfer realizing a PaymentMethod interface, PaymentService depending on PaymentMethod, and Order composed of OrderLine while associated with Customer." width="2480" height="1682" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Classes with operations, inheritance, composition (other UML routes elsewhere)</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/story-map.png" aria-label="View the Story map diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Story map</span><span>43 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/story-map.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/story-map.png" alt="User story map for a reporting tool's first release: four narrative activities from finding data to trusting it, walking-skeleton steps beneath each, and three release slices sliced by an MVP release-cut line, with the row-level-permissions story flagged as the riskiest bet in Release 2." width="2400" height="1258" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Narrative backbone sliced into releases, with the cut line</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/db-schema.png" aria-label="View the Database schema diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Database schema</span><span>44 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/db-schema.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/db-schema.png" alt="Physical database schema diagram showing five commerce tables with column-level foreign keys, SQL types, and constraint chips, including a cascading delete from orders into order_items and a billing schema group." width="2480" height="1288" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Physical tables: SQL types, constraints, indexes, column-level FKs</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/service-blueprint.png" aria-label="View the Service blueprint diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Service blueprint</span><span>45 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/service-blueprint.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/service-blueprint.png" alt="Service blueprint of a trial-to-paid path across five stages, with customer and frontstage actions above a line of visibility and a focal backstage dunning-job timeout under Hit the limit." width="2560" height="1442" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">What the customer does vs what the service hides, across stages</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/sbgn.png" aria-label="View the SBGN diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">SBGN</span><span>46 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/sbgn.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/sbgn.png" alt="Seven carotenoid species in cytosol cleaved by six processes; beta-carotene yields B-10-apo and B-ionone, with cryptoxanthin and zeaxanthin feeding the same products." width="2400" height="1442" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">A biological process as a bipartite species/process graph</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/requirement-traceability.png" aria-label="View the Requirement traceability diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Requirement traceability</span><span>47 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/requirement-traceability.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/requirement-traceability.png" alt="Three illustrative requirements trace from source notes to design elements and verification checks. The last requirement has no linked verification and is visibly marked as open." width="2400" height="1440" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Source requirements, design elements, and tests linked by stable IDs</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/event-modeling.png" aria-label="View the Event modeling diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Event modeling</span><span>48 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/event-modeling.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/event-modeling.png" alt="Three time-ordered stages. Each has a command, a resulting past-tense event, and a read model projected from that event." width="2400" height="1440" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">Commands, resulting events, and read models across ordered stages</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/steps.png" aria-label="View the Steps diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Steps</span><span>49 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/steps.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/steps.png" alt="Five equal stages move from framing and research through a focal synthesis step, then decision and release." width="2560" height="1442" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">A short ordered method with numbered stages, icons, and brief explanations</span></button>
      <button class="pl rise" type="button" data-full="assets/gallery/unit-grid.png" aria-label="View the Unit Grid diagram full size"><span class="top"><span class="t">Unit Grid</span><span>50 / 50</span></span><span class="pl-img"><picture><source srcset="assets/gallery/unit-grid.webp" type="image/webp"><img src="assets/gallery/unit-grid.png" alt="A ten by ten unit grid showing 64 completed release checks and 36 remaining checks. Each square represents one check." width="2076" height="810" loading="lazy"></picture><span class="zoom" aria-hidden="true"><em><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5"/><path d="M15.5 15.5L21 21"/><path d="M10.5 7.5v6M7.5 10.5h6"/></svg>Enlarge</em></span></span><span class="d">One bounded whole counted in equal discrete units out of 100</span></button>
    </div>
    <button class="m-more" type="button" data-more=".plates" aria-expanded="false">Show all 50 types</button>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ INSTALL ============ -->
<section id="install">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">Install</h2>
      <p class="note rise">Start with the first card. Click any card to copy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sheets">
      <div class="sheet lead rise" data-copy="npx skills add cathrynlavery/diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Any agent · Cursor and more<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy the npx skills install command">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy the npx skills install command"><code><span class="c"># one command, every skills host</span>
<span class="p">npx</span> skills add cathrynlavery/diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">For Cursor, Cline, Gemini CLI, Windsurf and other skills hosts. Update with <b>npx skills update diagram-design</b>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="/plugin marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design&#10;/plugin install diagram-design@diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Claude Code<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy Claude Code install commands">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy Claude Code install commands"><code><span class="c"># add + install</span>
<span class="p">/plugin</span> marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design
<span class="p">/plugin</span> install diagram-design@diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Then enable auto-update once in <b>/plugin → Marketplaces</b>.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="codex plugin marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design&#10;codex plugin add diagram-design@diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Codex<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy Codex install commands">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy Codex install commands"><code><span class="c"># add + install</span>
<span class="p">codex</span> plugin marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design
<span class="p">codex</span> plugin add diagram-design@diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Codex refreshes Git marketplaces at startup.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="pi install https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Pi<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy Pi install command">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy Pi install command"><code><span class="c"># install from GitHub</span>
<span class="p">pi</span> install https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Run <b>/reload</b> in an open Pi session.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="copilot plugin marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design&#10;copilot plugin install diagram-design@diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>GitHub Copilot<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy GitHub Copilot install commands">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy GitHub Copilot install commands"><code><span class="c"># add + install</span>
<span class="p">copilot</span> plugin marketplace add cathrynlavery/diagram-design
<span class="p">copilot</span> plugin install diagram-design@diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Confirm with <b>copilot skill list</b>, then ask for a diagram.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="droid plugin marketplace add https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design&#10;droid plugin install diagram-design@diagram-design --scope user">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Factory Droid<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy Factory Droid install commands">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy Factory Droid install commands"><code><span class="c"># add + install</span>
<span class="p">droid</span> plugin marketplace add https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design
<span class="p">droid</span> plugin install diagram-design@diagram-design --scope user</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Droid tracks updates by commit. Start a new session after updating.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="sheet rise" data-copy="git clone https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design.git&#10;qoder plugins install ./diagram-design">
        <div class="hd"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v14H4z"/><path d="M8 10l3 2-3 2M13 14h4"/></svg>Qoder<button class="cp" type="button" aria-label="Copy Qoder install commands">Copy</button></div>
        <pre role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Copy Qoder install commands"><code><span class="c"># clone + install</span>
<span class="p">git</span> clone https://github.com/cathrynlavery/diagram-design.git
<span class="p">qoder</span> plugins install ./diagram-design</code></pre>
        <div class="ft">Start a new task after installing. Qoder IDE takes a ZIP upload, see the README.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <button class="m-more" type="button" data-more=".sheets" aria-expanded="false">Codex, Pi, Copilot, Droid, Qoder</button>
    <p class="install-note rise">Kiro and OpenCode take the <b>skills/diagram-design</b> folder directly, see the README. Editable install? <b>git clone</b> the repo and symlink <b>skills/diagram-design</b>. Saved profiles in <b>~/.diagram-design/profiles/</b> survive updates.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ USE ============ -->
<section id="use">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <h2 class="rise">Then just ask</h2>
      <p class="note rise">Describe what you want in a sentence. No syntax, no config.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="use-grid">
      <div class="rise">
        <ul class="asks">
          <li><span class="q">&gt;_</span><span class="t">“Make me an <b>architecture diagram</b> of my app: frontend, backend, database, Redis cache.”</span></li>
          <li><span class="q">&gt;_</span><span class="t">“I need a <b>quadrant</b> of Q2 projects by impact vs effort.”</span></li>
          <li><span class="q">&gt;_</span><span class="t">“<b>onboard</b> diagram-design to <em>https://yoursite.com</em>”</span></li>
          <li><span class="q">&gt;_</span><span class="t">“<b>redraw</b> this <em>.drawio</em> file for my deck.”</span></li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tmpl">
          <div class="dim left" style="margin-bottom:12px" aria-hidden="true"><span>or start from a template</span></div>
          <pre><code><span class="c"># copy a scaffold and edit</span>
cp skills/diagram-design/assets/template.html my-diagram.html</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="dogfood rise">
        <figcaption>Fig. 03 · one turn<span>no syntax · one file</span></figcaption>
        <div class="term plate reg-b">
          <div class="term-bar">agent session<span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
          <pre class="term-body"><code><span class="p">&gt;</span> make me an architecture diagram of my app
<span class="c">  reads your brand · picks type: architecture</span>
<span class="c">  states the plan, then draws</span>
<span class="ok">wrote</span> architecture.html<span class="c">  one file, opens offline</span></code></pre>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</main>


<div class="modal" id="imodal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Diagram, full size" hidden>
  <button class="modal-close" id="iclose" type="button" aria-label="Close image"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 5l14 14M19 5L5 19"/></svg></button>
  <div class="modal-frame plate reg-b">
    <div class="imodal-cap" id="imodal-cap"><span class="t"></span><span>Esc or click outside to close</span></div>
    <img id="imodal-img" src="" alt="">
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ============ FOOTER ============ -->
<footer>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="by">Made by <a href="https://littlemight.com?utm_source=diagramdesign.dev&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=footer">Cathryn Lavery</a>.</p>
